# /sdd-swarm

Purpose:
  Execute the SW1 chain — parallel micro-unit delivery with a
  defect-focus loop. Macro-sequential, micro-parallel.

Owns: commands\sdd-swarm.sdd
Description:
  Run the SW1 swarm pipeline: decompose each of the 16 stages into
  micro-units, dispatch independent units to parallel subagents,
  merge, verify, and loop on defects with a narrow focus pass.

Usage:
  /sdd-swarm
  /sdd-swarm --stage <key>
  /sdd-swarm --board
  /sdd-swarm --focus MU-<id>
  /sdd-swarm --status
  /sdd-swarm --dry-run

Options:
  --stage <key>   Start from a specific SW1 stage (default: DB)
  --board         Combined parallel progress view (all stages +
                  micro-unit states + defect queue + focus iterations)
  --focus MU-<id> Re-dispatch one unit in FOCUS mode with a narrow
                  context pack (defect + unit + BEFORE/CHANGE/AFTER)
  --status        Show current swarm run state
  --dry-run       Plan the run without dispatching subagents

Mode: SUPERVISED

InitialLoad (Phase 151 — EXPAND protocol):
  - .sdd/INDEX.sdd (routing only)
  - .sdd/chains/swarm.sdd (SW1 chain)
  - .sdd/workflow/step-keys.sdd (SW1 dictionary — SW1 group)
  - .sdd/workflow/micro-unit.sdd (MICRO-UNIT entity + budget rules)
  - .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/state.sdd (saved swarm state, [SF1])
  Stage specs and gate details load on EXPAND only.

StatefulExecution ([CMD6]):
  1. DISCOVER — read saved swarm state; if none, initialize a new run
  2. ANALYZE — locate current_stage and first incomplete micro-unit
  3. EXECUTE ONLY the current SWARM cycle step for the current stage
  4. VERIFY — DONE criteria per swarm.sdd [SW1-4]
  5. SAVE STATE — update .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/state.sdd
  6. STOP

SwarmCycle (per stage — execute ONE cycle step per invocation):
  1. DECOMPOSE — stage scope -> micro-units (MU-XXX); build DAG;
     mark PARALLEL_READY units
  2. DISPATCH — supervisor dispatches PARALLEL_READY units to parallel
     subagents; context reassembled via handoff (NOT copied)
  3. MERGE — fan-in; conflicts detected and resolved; failed units isolated
  4. VERIFY — stage tests run inside Docker ([R102]); result per unit
  5. DEFECT-CHECK — scan results -> defect catalog (DEF-XXX -> MU-XXX)
  6. FOCUS LOOP — narrow re-dispatch + re-verify per defect;
     bounds: arm cap 10, error spiral 3, LOOP_SCORE >= 60 strategy
     change, >= 90 escalate
  7. Stage DONE -> next macro-stage

FocusLoopBounds:
  arm_cap: 10            # max focus iterations per stage
  error_spiral: 3        # 3 consecutive typed failures -> wrap/escalate
  loop_score_high: 60    # strategy change required
  loop_score_crit: 90    # escalate to human
  rule: per LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd [LP11-LP13], [SP1]-[SP4], [SUP-03]

Output:
  Default:
    [swarm_mode: cycle]
    [run_id: <id>]  [flow_version: 2]  [current_stage: <key>]
    [last_completed: <key>]  [first_incomplete: <key>]
    [micro_units: <count by state>]  [defects: <count>]
    [action: execute_one_cycle_step]
    [result: <cycle outcome + DONE-evidence>]

  --board:
    Combined view — all 16 stages with state, per-stage micro-unit
    counts by lifecycle state, defect queue (DEF-XXX -> MU-XXX),
    focus iteration log, token_totals.

  --status:
    [run_id] [current_stage] [stage_states] [defects] [focus_iterations]
    [token_totals] [loop_guards]

Rules:
  [SWARM-01] /sdd-swarm continues from saved state, never memory.
  [SWARM-02] One SWARM cycle step per invocation — never execute a
        future stage early (FLOW VIOLATION, [CMD6]).
  [SWARM-03] DL1 is untouched; SW1 is a separate chain ([SW1-7]).
  [SWARM-04] REL is terminal and requires human approval ([CMD3], [RS1]).
  [SWARM-05] All test execution runs inside Docker ([R102]).
  [SWARM-06] State is runtime-only, never committed ([R103]).
  [SWARM-07] UTF-8 only ([R99]); no AI signatures in commits ([R103]).

